        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "2d2fc632-247b-540a-8c4c-979650f25e86",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: One Summer Love, Dragonfly, Law and Disorder, Bang the Drum Slowly, Alice, Sweet Alice, Red Riding Hood, The Emperor's New Clothes, The Tale of Peter Rabbit\n- People: Gilbert Cates, N. Richard Nash, Beau Bridges, Susan Sarandon, Mildred Dunnock, Ann Wedgeworth, Stephen J. Lawrence, Ivan Passer, Carroll O'Connor, Ernest Borgnine, Karen Black, Marlo Thomas, Robert De Niro, Isabella Rossellini, Craig T. Nelson, Michael Korie, Sid Caesar, Robert Morse, Carol Burnett, Sheldon Harnick\n- Television and Music Projects: Sesame Street, Free to Be... You and Me, Three's Company, Evening Shade\n- Awards: Emmy Awards, Peabody Award, Paris International Festival of Fantasy and Science Fiction music award\n\nFacts:\n- Ann Wedgeworth was born on January 21, 1934, and is an American character actress.\n- Law and Disorder is a 1974 American comedy-drama film directed by Ivan Passer and starring Carroll O'Connor, Ernest Borgnine, Ann Wedgeworth, and Karen Black.\n- One Summer Love, originally titled Dragonfly, is a 1976 romantic drama film directed by Gilbert Cates from a screenplay by N. Richard Nash.\n- One Summer Love stars Beau Bridges and Susan Sarandon and features Mildred Dunnock and Ann Wedgeworth.\n- Stephen J. Lawrence composed the score for the 1976 film One Summer Love, also known as Dragonfly.\n- Stephen J. Lawrence composed more than 300 songs and scores for Sesame Street and won three Emmy Awards for Outstanding Achievement in Music Direction and Composition for that work.\n- Stephen J. Lawrence composed the title song and four other songs for Marlo Thomas's Free to Be... You and Me, which became a million-selling record, book, and Emmy Award- and Peabody Award-winning ABC television special.\n- Stephen J. Lawrence composed the million-selling Gold Record You Take My Breath Away.\n- Stephen J. Lawrence scored the film Bang the Drum Slowly and the cult horror film Alice, Sweet Alice, which won the music award at the Paris International Festival of Fantasy and Science Fiction.\n- Stephen J. Lawrence composed the songs and score for the 1989 live-action movie musical Red Riding Hood, starring Isabella Rossellini and Craig T. Nelson, with lyrics by Michael Korie.\n- Stephen J. Lawrence composed songs for the live-action movie musical The Emperor's New Clothes, starring Sid Caesar and Robert Morse.\n- Stephen J. Lawrence composed the songs and score for the HBO animated musical The Tale of Peter Rabbit, starring Carol Burnett, with lyrics by Sheldon Harnick.\n- Ann Wedgeworth is known for her roles as Lana Shields in Three's Company and Merleen Elldridge in Evening Shade.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
